    "['unit [unit_number] protocols [protocol_name] area [area_number]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo ipv6 ospfv3 1 area 0.0.0.0 interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0', 'parent_command': ['interface [interface-name]'], 'root': 'interface [interface-name]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper commands to Huawei equivalent commands:\\n\\n##\\nundo ipv6 ospfv3 1 area 0.0.0.0 interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\nundo ipv6 ospfv3 1 area 0.0.0.0 interface GigabitEthernet0/0/4\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. In Huawei, OSPFv3 is configured with a process ID (1 in this example)\\n2. The interface naming follows Huawei\\'s convention (GigabitEthernetX/X/X)\\n3. The \"undo\" command is Huawei\\'s equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"delete\" for removing configurations\\n4. The area is specified in dotted decimal format (0.0.0.0) similar to Juniper\\'s area 0', 'trans_template': 'undo ipv6 ospfv3 1 area 0.0.0.0 interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo ipv6 ospfv3 1 area 0.0.0.0 interface GigabitEthernet0/0/4', 'parent_command': ['interface [interface-name]'], 'root': 'interface [interface-name]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper commands to Huawei equivalent commands:\\n\\n##\\nundo ipv6 ospfv3 1 area 0.0.0.0 interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\nundo ipv6 ospfv3 1 area 0.0.0.0 interface GigabitEthernet0/0/4\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. In Huawei, OSPFv3 is configured with a process ID (1 in this example)\\n2. The interface naming follows Huawei\\'s convention (GigabitEthernetX/X/X)\\n3. The \"undo\" command is Huawei\\'s equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"delete\" for removing configurations\\n4. The area is specified in dotted decimal format (0.0.0.0) similar to Juniper\\'s area 0', 'trans_template': 'undo ipv6 ospfv3 1 area 0.0.0.0 interface GigabitEthernet0/0/4'}]]": 1,
    "['unit [parameter2] protocols [parameter3] [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo pim ipv6 sparse-mode', 'parent_command': ['interface [interface-name]'], 'root': 'interface [interface-name]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI configuration for the Juniper commands you provided:\\n\\n##\\nundo pim ipv6 sparse-mode\\n##\\n\\nNote: In HUAWEI devices, PIM configuration is typically done at the interface level, and there\\'s no direct \"unit\" concept like Juniper. The \"undo pim ipv6 sparse-mode\" command would be applied to the corresponding interfaces (in this case, the IPv6-enabled interfaces equivalent to ge-0/0/0 and ge-0/0/4). The exact interface names might differ (like GigabitEthernet0/0/0 in HUAWEI).', 'trans_template': 'undo pim ipv6 sparse-mode'}]]": 1,
