    "['unit [unit_number] protocols [protocol_name] area [area_number]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo ospfv3 0 enable interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0', 'parent_command': ['interface [interface-name]'], 'root': 'interface [interface-name]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper commands to Huawei equivalent commands:\\n\\n##\\nundo ospfv3 0 enable interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\nundo ospfv3 0 enable interface GigabitEthernet0/0/4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Huawei devices, OSPFv3 is configured under interface view with the command `ospfv3 <process-id> enable`\\n- The `undo` command is used to remove configuration (equivalent to Juniper's `delete`)\\n- The interface naming follows Huawei's convention (GigabitEthernetX/X/X)\\n- The area 0 is specified in the process ID (0 in this case)\", 'trans_template': 'undo ospfv3 0 enable interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo ospfv3 0 enable interface GigabitEthernet0/0/4', 'parent_command': ['interface [interface-name]'], 'root': 'interface [interface-name]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper commands to Huawei equivalent commands:\\n\\n##\\nundo ospfv3 0 enable interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\nundo ospfv3 0 enable interface GigabitEthernet0/0/4\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Huawei devices, OSPFv3 is configured under interface view with the command `ospfv3 <process-id> enable`\\n- The `undo` command is used to remove configuration (equivalent to Juniper's `delete`)\\n- The interface naming follows Huawei's convention (GigabitEthernetX/X/X)\\n- The area 0 is specified in the process ID (0 in this case)\", 'trans_template': 'undo ospfv3 0 enable interface GigabitEthernet0/0/4'}]]": 1,
